{%- import "macros.njk" as m with context -%}
{%- set first = history.years | first -%}
{%- set latest = history.years | last -%}
{#- The source line under the chart and the table, built once here and handed to the view by the build and by the browser. -#}
{%- set historySources = { rates: "the Department for Work and Pensions' benefit and pension rates", decisions: "the explanatory memorandum to each Up-rating Order", listed_url: "/history/#decisions", prices: "the Office for National Statistics' Consumer Prices Index, series D7BT", prices_url: history.sources.prices_index_url, checked: (history.checked_date | dateText) } -%}
<h1>State Pension history explorer</h1>

<p class="lede">The full rates since 2010 as a chart and table: in cash, in buying power or against earnings, with a calculation of what another rule would have produced. The record itself is on <a href="/history/">the history page</a>. <a href="/tools/">All tools</a>.</p>

<section class="tool" aria-labelledby="explorer">
  <h2 id="explorer">Explore the history</h2>

  <p class="js-only">Choose a pension, a range of years and how to show the amounts. You can add a calculation of what another rule would have produced from the first year you choose.</p>

  <div class="no-js-only">
    {% call m.note("The explorer needs JavaScript", 3, "the-explorer-needs-javascript") %}
    <p>The form is not available, because JavaScript is off or did not load. <span class="if-script-failed">The script for this form did not run to the end, though the page's other scripts did. Reload the page; if that does not help, <a href="/sources-and-method/#report-an-error">report it</a>.</span> The chart and table below show the basic State Pension in cash. The full record is in the table and the download on <a href="/history/#decisions">the history page</a>.</p>
    {% endcall %}
  </div>

  <div class="tool-layout">
  <form id="history-form" class="js-only" novalidate>
    <fieldset>
      <legend>What to show</legend>
      <div class="fields">
        <div class="field">
          <label for="history-series">Pension</label>
          <span class="hint" id="history-series-hint">The new State Pension starts in 2016/17.</span>
          <select id="history-series" name="history-series" aria-describedby="history-series-hint">
            <option value="basic">Full basic State Pension</option>
            <option value="new">Full new State Pension</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="history-measure">Show amounts as</label>
          <span class="hint" id="history-measure-hint">Cash is the money of each year. Buying power is in the prices of the last year shown. Compared with earnings is an index, first year shown&nbsp;=&nbsp;100.</span>
          <select id="history-measure" name="history-measure" aria-describedby="history-measure-hint">
            <option value="cash">Cash</option>
            <option value="real">Buying power</option>
            <option value="earnings">Compared with earnings</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="history-from">First year</label>
          <span class="error" id="history-error" role="alert"></span>
          <select id="history-from" name="history-from" aria-describedby="history-error"></select>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="history-to">Last year</label>
          <select id="history-to" name="history-to"></select>
        </div>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="history-rule">Add a calculation under another rule</label>
          <span class="hint" id="history-rule-hint">Applied every year from the published rate of the first year you chose. It leaves out the exceptions Parliament made, such as setting aside the earnings part in 2022/23.</span>
          <select id="history-rule" name="history-rule" aria-describedby="history-rule-hint">
            <option value="">None</option>
            <option value="triple-lock">Triple lock, no exceptions</option>
            <option value="double-lock">Double lock, no exceptions</option>
            <option value="earnings">Earnings link</option>
            <option value="prices">Prices link</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="buttons">
        <button type="button" class="secondary" id="history-download">Download the table shown (CSV)</button>
        <button type="button" class="secondary" id="history-copy">Copy the table shown</button>
      </div>
    </fieldset>
  </form>
  <div class="tool-summary js-only">
    <h3 id="history-glance-heading">At a glance</h3>
    <div id="history-glance">
      <p>The result appears here as you fill in the form.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  </div>

  <p class="visually-hidden" role="status" id="history-status"></p>

  <div class="result" id="history-result">
    {{ { years: history.years, series: "basic", from: first.tax_year, to: latest.tax_year, measure: "cash", rule: "", sources: historySources } | renderHistory | safe }}
  </div>

  <h3 id="how-the-measures-are-worked-out">How the measures are worked out</h3>
  <dl>
    <dt>Cash</dt> <dd>The published rate.</dd>
    <dt>Buying power</dt> <dd>The published rate × the price index for the last year shown ÷ the price index for that year. The index is the Consumer Prices Index level for the September before each rate took effect.</dd>
    <dt>Compared with earnings</dt> <dd>The rise in the rate since the first year shown, divided by the rise in earnings over the same years. The rise in earnings is built from the figures used in each decision. It is an index, not a share of any pay figure in pounds.</dd>
    <dt>A calculation under another rule</dt> <dd>The rule is applied year by year from the published rate of the first year, using the prices and earnings figures recorded for each year's decision, with rounding to the nearest 5p and no fall in pounds. It does not apply the special rules of exceptional years.</dd>
  </dl>
  <div class="source">
    <p>Source for the price index: <a href="{{ history.sources.prices_index_url }}">{{ history.sources.prices_index }}</a> Checked against the source on {{ history.checked_date | dateText | safe }}.</p>
  </div>
  <p><a href="/sources-and-method/#models">Full method, reference examples and limits</a>. For future years, which are hypothetical, use the <a href="/reform-options/compare/">rule comparison</a>.</p>

  <script type="application/json" id="history-data">{{ { years: history.years, sources: historySources } | json | safe }}</script>
  <script type="module" src="/assets/js/tools/history.js"></script>
</section>
